  "rationale": "Pareto target: latency (epsilon 2000ms). Baseline latency_median=37798ms, output_chars_mean=21325. Round 1 attacked citations already; summary text is the next largest output component (25 sections \u00d7 ~2 sentences \u00d7 ~25 words \u2248 1250 words of summary \u2248 7500 chars). Changing from '1-3 sentences, prefer 1-2' to 'strictly 1 sentence (15-30 words), 2nd sentence only for a named fact that would otherwise be lost' plus a ban on lead-in phrases ('This section...') cuts an estimated 15-20% of summary chars \u2192 ~2000-3000 char output reduction \u2192 ~2500-4500ms latency drop, clearing the 2000ms epsilon. All verbatim-preservation guards remain (legal terms, cross-refs, thresholds, dates, parties) and are expanded explicitly to dollar amounts/percentages/time windows \u2014 this protects the summary_quality judge (currently 0.887), which rewards faithfulness and precision over length. Predicted summary_quality delta: -0.00 to -0.02, well inside the 0.03 quality epsilon. No clash with other skills: hierarchy/citations/exclusions/output_schema do not constrain summary sentence count or wording. Not a repeat of Round 1 (that touched citations.md source_text length; this touches section_summary.md sentence/word cap). schema_adherence and output_json_valid are unchanged (field names/types unchanged).",
